# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and in every working copy.
#
# This is not cosmetic here. `init` and `sync` record a sha256 for every file they write into a
# project and refuse to overwrite a file whose hash no longer matches, so that work done by hand
# is never destroyed. A checkout that rewrote LF to CRLF would change those bytes without anyone
# touching the files, and every one of them would be reported as edited by hand — a failure that
# looks like a bug in the hash rule rather than a line-ending difference.
*		text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the content that ends up in that comparison: blueprints and skill markdown, the
# generated index, workflow and config files, licence texts. `text=auto` would almost certainly
# classify these correctly on its own, but "almost certainly" is not a good basis for a rule whose
# failure is silent.
*.md		text eol=lf
*.txt		text eol=lf
*.json		text eol=lf
*.yml		text eol=lf
*.yaml		text eol=lf
*.toml		text eol=lf
*.py		text eol=lf
*.html		text eol=lf
*.css		text eol=lf
LICENSE			text eol=lf
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES	text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
